IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ea-core`
IMPORT `ea-definitions`
IMPORT `sgia-interpretation-time`

-- Employment Act 1968 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation
-- "version in force from 5/12/2025" -- LAYER 1, PART 3 (a): ss 20 to 25, the salary
-- period, the salary for an incomplete month, and when, where and to whom salary is paid.
--
-- Source text: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore
-- Statutes Online (inputs/EmA1968.txt).  It is not the official text.  Every
-- `-- src:` line copies a line of that file (script-generated); every quotation in
-- a FALSE-kind or NOTHING-kind comment is a phrase of it (checked by a script).
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the Act gives in its
-- own words.  NOTHING means the Act does not answer on these facts and is never to
-- be read as no.  "marginal (a)" or "marginal (b)" marks the branches that rest on
-- one of the two readings for a lawyer (NOTES.md).
--
-- PERIODS OF DAYS.  Sections 21, 22, 23, 24 and 66 count days "after" an event.  They
-- are read as a period of days from the event, which the Interpretation Act 1965
-- s 50 counts (staged in DEPENDENCIES as sgia-interpretation-time): the day of the
-- event is left out, and a last day that is a Sunday or a public holiday moves to
-- the next day that is not (NOTES.md, fork F-PERIODS).  The public holidays are a
-- list the caller gives, because the Holidays Act is not among the sources.  Where
-- section 22 or 23 has a rule of its own about holidays, its own rule governs.

§ `Employment Act 1968 -- Part 3 Payment of salary, ss 20 to 25`

§§ `s 20 Fixation of salary period`

-- src:1271 | 20.—(1) An employer may fix periods (called for the purpose of
-- src:1272 | this Act salary periods) in respect of which salary earned is payable.
@ref s 20(1) (src:1271-1272)
GIVEN `the person is the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 20(1) the employer may fix periods in respect of which salary earned is payable` MEANS
    IF `the person is the employer`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An employer may fix periods"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- "A month" is a calendar month (Interpretation Act 1965 s 2(1)): a period that starts
-- on a day exceeds a month if it runs past the day before the same day of the next month;
-- where the next month has no such day (a period starting on the 31st), the month is
-- taken to end on the next month's last day (NOTES.md, fork F-20(2)).
-- src:1274 | (2) A salary period must not exceed one month.
@ref s 20(2) (src:1274-1274)
GIVEN period IS A `Period of days`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 20(2) the salary period does not exceed one month` MEANS
    IF period's `last day` LESS THAN `the first day after the month`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A salary period must not exceed one month" -- marginal (a)
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `the same day of the next month` MEANS Date (DATE_DAY (period's `first day`)) ((DATE_MONTH (period's `first day`)) PLUS 1) (DATE_YEAR (period's `first day`))
        `the first of the month after the next` MEANS Date 1 ((DATE_MONTH (period's `first day`)) PLUS 2) (DATE_YEAR (period's `first day`))
        `the first day after the month` MEANS IF `the same day of the next month` LESS THAN `the first of the month after the next` THEN `the same day of the next month` ELSE `the first of the month after the next`

-- src:1276 | (3) In the absence of a salary period so fixed, the salary period is
-- src:1277 | deemed to be one month.
@ref s 20(3) (src:1276-1277)
GIVEN `the employer has fixed a salary period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 20(3) the salary period is deemed to be one month` MEANS
    IF NOT `the employer has fixed a salary period`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In the absence of a salary period so fixed" -- marginal (a)
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 20A Computation of salary for incomplete month's work`

-- The days required to work for 5 hours or less count as half a day.
-- src:1306 | (2) In calculating the number of days actually worked by an
-- src:1307 | employee in a month under subsection (1), any day on which an
-- src:1308 | employee is required to work for 5 hours or less under his or her
-- src:1309 | contract of service is regarded as half a day.
@ref s 20A(2) (src:1306-1309)
GIVEN `the number of days actually worked on which the employee was required to work for more than 5 hours` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of days actually worked on which the employee was required to work for 5 hours or less` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 20A(2) the number of days actually worked` MEANS
    `the number of days actually worked on which the employee was required to work for more than 5 hours` PLUS (`the number of days actually worked on which the employee was required to work for 5 hours or less` DIVIDED BY 2)

-- src:1281 | 20A.—(1) If a monthly-rated employee has not completed a whole
-- src:1282 | month of service because —
-- src:1284 | (a) he or she commenced employment after the first day of the
-- src:1285 | month;
-- src:1287 | (b) his or her employment was terminated before the end of the
-- src:1288 | month;
-- src:1290 | (c) he or she took leave of absence without pay for one or more
-- src:1291 | days of the month; or
-- src:1293 | (d) he or she took leave of absence to perform his or her
-- src:1294 | national service under the Enlistment Act 1970,
-- src:1296 | the salary due to him or her for that month is to be calculated in
-- src:1297 | accordance with the following formula:
-- src:1299 | Monthly gross rate of pay
-- src:1301 | Number of days on which the x Number of days the employee
-- src:1302 | employee is required to work actually worked in that month.
-- src:1304 | in that month
@ref s 20A(1) (src:1281-1304)
GIVEN `the employee is monthly-rated` IS A BOOLEAN
      `commenced employment after the first day of the month` IS A BOOLEAN
      `employment was terminated before the end of the month` IS A BOOLEAN
      `took leave of absence without pay for one or more days of the month` IS A BOOLEAN
      `took leave of absence to perform national service under the Enlistment Act 1970` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 20A(1) the employee has not completed a whole month of service for a reason in paragraphs (a) to (d)` MEANS
    IF `the employee is monthly-rated` AND (`commenced employment after the first day of the month` OR `employment was terminated before the end of the month` OR `took leave of absence without pay for one or more days of the month` OR `took leave of absence to perform national service under the Enlistment Act 1970`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a monthly-rated employee has not completed a whole month of service because" -- ruled 2026-11-05: an unmet "if" (the employee is not monthly-rated, or none of the reasons in paragraphs (a) to (d) holds)
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- The formula: the monthly gross rate of pay, divided by the number of days on which the
-- employee is required to work in the month, times the number of days actually worked.
-- The monthly gross rate is the keel's gross rate of pay for a pay record whose amounts
-- are for a month.
@ref s 20A(1) (src:1296-1304)
GIVEN pay IS A `Pay for a period`
      `the number of days on which the employee is required to work in that month` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of days the employee actually worked in that month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 20A(1) the salary due for the month` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the formula is written for the "Monthly gross rate of pay"; an amount fixed for another unit is not one
        IF NOT (pay's `the amounts are for` EQUALS `Pay is fixed for each month`) THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the formula divides by the number of days the employee is required to work in the month, and gives no answer for none
        IF `the number of days on which the employee is required to work in that month` AT MOST 0 THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST ((`s 2(1) "gross rate of pay" the amount` pay DIVIDED BY `the number of days on which the employee is required to work in that month`) TIMES `the number of days the employee actually worked in that month`)

§§ `s 21 Time of payment`

-- The count is from the last day of the salary period (the event); "the 7th day after"
-- is the 7th day of the period of days from it.
-- src:1316 | 21.—(1) Salary earned by an employee under a contract of service,
-- src:1317 | other than additional payments for overtime work, must be paid
-- src:1318 | before the expiry of the 7th day after the last day of the salary period
-- src:1319 | in respect of which the salary is payable.
@ref s 21(1) (src:1316-1319)
GIVEN `the last day of the salary period` IS A DATE
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 21(1) the last day before the expiry of which the salary must be paid` MEANS
    `the last day of a period of days from the event` `the last day of the salary period` 7 `the public holidays` FALSE

@ref s 21(1) (src:1316-1319)
GIVEN `the last day of the salary period` IS A DATE
      `the day the salary was paid` IS A DATE
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
      `the payment is an additional payment for overtime work` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(1) the salary was paid before the expiry of the 7th day after the last day of the salary period` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "other than additional payments for overtime work", which subsection (2) deals with
        IF `the payment is an additional payment for overtime work` THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `s 21(1) the last day before the expiry of which the salary must be paid` `the last day of the salary period` `the public holidays`
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the count of days comes from the Interpretation Act module, which gives no answer
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST last THEN JUST (`the day the salary was paid` AT MOST last)

DECLARE `s 21(1) Actor` IS ONE OF
    `s 21(1) the employer`

DECLARE `s 21(1) Action` IS ONE OF
    `s 21(1) pay the salary earned`

-- The duty of subsection (1) as a regulative rule.  The clock counts days from the last day
-- of the salary period; the deadline is the number of days given (7 when no holiday moves it).
@ref s 21(1) (src:1316-1319)
GIVEN `the number of days from the last day of the salary period to the last day for payment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 21(1) Actor` `s 21(1) Action`
`s 21(1) the employer's duty to pay the salary earned` MEANS
    PARTY `s 21(1) the employer`
    MUST `s 21(1) pay the salary earned`
    WITHIN `the number of days from the last day of the salary period to the last day for payment`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 21(1) the employer` BECAUSE "the salary was not paid before the expiry of the 7th day after the last day of the salary period"

-- src:1321 | (2) Additional payments for overtime work must be paid not later
-- src:1322 | than 14 days after the last day of the salary period during which the
-- src:1323 | overtime work was performed.
@ref s 21(2) (src:1321-1323)
GIVEN `the last day of the salary period during which the overtime work was performed` IS A DATE
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 21(2) the last day by which the additional payments for overtime work must be paid` MEANS
    `the last day of a period of days from the event` `the last day of the salary period during which the overtime work was performed` 14 `the public holidays` FALSE

@ref s 21(2) (src:1321-1323)
GIVEN `the last day of the salary period during which the overtime work was performed` IS A DATE
      `the day the additional payments for overtime work were paid` IS A DATE
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21(2) the additional payments for overtime work were paid not later than 14 days after the last day of the salary period` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 21(2) the last day by which the additional payments for overtime work must be paid` `the last day of the salary period during which the overtime work was performed` `the public holidays`
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the count of days comes from the Interpretation Act module, which gives no answer
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST last THEN JUST (`the day the additional payments for overtime work were paid` AT MOST last)

DECLARE `s 21(2) Actor` IS ONE OF
    `s 21(2) the employer`

DECLARE `s 21(2) Action` IS ONE OF
    `s 21(2) pay the additional payments for overtime work`

@ref s 21(2) (src:1321-1323)
GIVEN `the number of days from the last day of the salary period to the last day for payment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 21(2) Actor` `s 21(2) Action`
`s 21(2) the employer's duty to pay the additional payments for overtime work` MEANS
    PARTY `s 21(2) the employer`
    MUST `s 21(2) pay the additional payments for overtime work`
    WITHIN `the number of days from the last day of the salary period to the last day for payment`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 21(2) the employer` BECAUSE "the additional payments for overtime work were not paid within 14 days after the last day of the salary period"

-- src:1325 | (3) The total salary due to an employee on completion of his or her
-- src:1326 | contract of service must be paid to him or her on completion of the
-- src:1327 | contract.
@ref s 21(3) (src:1325-1327)
GIVEN `the day the contract of service was completed` IS A DATE
      `the day the total salary due was paid` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 21(3) the total salary due was paid on completion of the contract of service` MEANS
    `the day the total salary due was paid` AT MOST `the day the contract of service was completed`

§§ `s 22 Payment on dismissal`

-- "within 3 days thereafter, not being a rest day or public holiday or other holiday": read
-- as three days, the day of payment being one that is not a rest day, a public holiday or
-- another holiday (NOTES.md, fork F-22).  The employer's own rule here governs, and the
-- Interpretation Act's s 50 is not used for it.
-- src:1331 | 22. Subject to the provisions of this Act, the total salary and any
-- src:1332 | sum due to an employee who has been dismissed must be paid on the
-- src:1333 | day of dismissal or, if this is not possible, within 3 days thereafter, not
-- src:1334 | being a rest day or public holiday or other holiday.
@ref s 22 (src:1331-1334)
GIVEN `the day of dismissal` IS A DATE
      `it was not possible to pay on the day of dismissal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the days that are a rest day, a public holiday or another holiday` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 22 the last day on which the total salary and any sum due must be paid` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `it was not possible to pay on the day of dismissal` THEN JUST `the day of dismissal`
        IF NOT (elem (`the day of dismissal` PLUS 3) `the days that are a rest day, a public holiday or another holiday`) THEN JUST (`the day of dismissal` PLUS 3)
        IF NOT (elem (`the day of dismissal` PLUS 2) `the days that are a rest day, a public holiday or another holiday`) THEN JUST (`the day of dismissal` PLUS 2)
        IF NOT (elem (`the day of dismissal` PLUS 1) `the days that are a rest day, a public holiday or another holiday`) THEN JUST (`the day of dismissal` PLUS 1)
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): each of the 3 days is a rest day or a holiday, and the text gives no later day
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

@ref s 22 (src:1331-1334)
GIVEN `the day of dismissal` IS A DATE
      `the day the total salary and any sum due was paid` IS A DATE
      `it was not possible to pay on the day of dismissal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the days that are a rest day, a public holiday or another holiday` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 22 the total salary and any sum due was paid on the day of dismissal or, if that was not possible, within 3 days after, on a day that is not a rest day or holiday` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the day the total salary and any sum due was paid` EQUALS `the day of dismissal` THEN TRUE
        IF `it was not possible to pay on the day of dismissal` AND (`the day the total salary and any sum due was paid` GREATER THAN `the day of dismissal`) AND (`the day the total salary and any sum due was paid` AT MOST (`the day of dismissal` PLUS 3)) AND (NOT (elem `the day the total salary and any sum due was paid` `the days that are a rest day, a public holiday or another holiday`)) THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE `s 22 Actor` IS ONE OF
    `s 22 the employer`

DECLARE `s 22 Action` IS ONE OF
    `s 22 pay the total salary and any sum due to the dismissed employee`

@ref s 22 (src:1331-1334)
GIVEN `the number of days from the day of dismissal to the last day for payment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 22 Actor` `s 22 Action`
`s 22 the employer's duty to pay on dismissal` MEANS
    PARTY `s 22 the employer`
    MUST `s 22 pay the total salary and any sum due to the dismissed employee`
    WITHIN `the number of days from the day of dismissal to the last day for payment`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 22 the employer` BECAUSE "the total salary and any sum due was not paid on the day of dismissal or within 3 days after"

§§ `s 23 Payment on termination by employee`

-- src:1340 | 23.—(1) Subject to the provisions of this Act, the total salary due to
-- src:1341 | an employee who terminates his or her contract of service with his or
-- src:1342 | her employer under section 11, or after giving due notice to the
-- src:1343 | employer as required under section 10, must be paid to the employee
-- src:1344 | on the day on which the contract of service is terminated.
@ref s 23(1) (src:1340-1344)
GIVEN `the employee terminates the contract of service under section 11, or after giving due notice under section 10` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the contract of service is terminated` IS A DATE
      `the day the total salary due was paid` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23(1) the total salary due was paid on the day on which the contract of service was terminated` MEANS
    IF `the employee terminates the contract of service under section 11, or after giving due notice under section 10`
    THEN JUST (`the day the total salary due was paid` AT MOST `the day the contract of service is terminated`)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an employee who terminates his or her contract of service with his or her employer under section 11, or after giving due notice to the employer as required under section 10"
    ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `s 23(1) Actor` IS ONE OF
    `s 23(1) the employer`

DECLARE `s 23(1) Action` IS ONE OF
    `s 23(1) pay the total salary due to the employee on the day on which the contract of service is terminated`

@ref s 23(1) (src:1340-1344)
GIVEN `the employee terminates the contract of service under section 11, or after giving due notice under section 10` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 23(1) Actor` `s 23(1) Action`
`s 23(1) the employer's duty to pay on the day the contract of service is terminated` MEANS
    IF `the employee terminates the contract of service under section 11, or after giving due notice under section 10`
    THEN PARTY `s 23(1) the employer`
         MUST `s 23(1) pay the total salary due to the employee on the day on which the contract of service is terminated`
         WITHIN 0
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `s 23(1) the employer` BECAUSE "the total salary due was not paid on the day on which the contract of service was terminated"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:1346 | (2) Subject to the provisions of this Act, the total salary due to an
-- src:1347 | employee who terminates his or her contract of service without giving
-- src:1348 | prior notice to his or her employer as required under section 10, or, if
-- src:1349 | notice has already been given under that section, but the employee
-- src:1350 | terminates his or her contract of service without waiting for the expiry
-- src:1351 | of the notice, must be paid to the employee before the expiry of the
-- src:1352 | 7th day after the day on which the employee terminates his or her
-- src:1353 | contract of service.
@ref s 23(2) (src:1346-1353)
GIVEN `the day the employee terminates the contract of service` IS A DATE
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 23(2) the last day before the expiry of which the total salary due must be paid` MEANS
    `the last day of a period of days from the event` `the day the employee terminates the contract of service` 7 `the public holidays` FALSE

@ref s 23(2) (src:1346-1353)
GIVEN `the employee terminates the contract of service without giving prior notice as required under section 10, or without waiting for the notice to expire` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the employee terminates the contract of service` IS A DATE
      `the day the total salary due was paid` IS A DATE
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 23(2) the total salary due was paid before the expiry of the 7th day after the day on which the employee terminated the contract of service` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an employee who terminates his or her contract of service without giving prior notice ... or ... without waiting for the expiry of the notice"
        IF NOT `the employee terminates the contract of service without giving prior notice as required under section 10, or without waiting for the notice to expire` THEN NOTHING
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `s 23(2) the last day before the expiry of which the total salary due must be paid` `the day the employee terminates the contract of service` `the public holidays`
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the count of days comes from the Interpretation Act module, which gives no answer
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST last THEN JUST (`the day the total salary due was paid` AT MOST last)

DECLARE `s 23(2) Actor` IS ONE OF
    `s 23(2) the employer`

DECLARE `s 23(2) Action` IS ONE OF
    `s 23(2) pay the total salary due to the employee`

@ref s 23(2) (src:1346-1353)
GIVEN `the number of days from the day the employee terminates the contract of service to the last day for payment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 23(2) Actor` `s 23(2) Action`
`s 23(2) the employer's duty to pay after the employee terminates without notice` MEANS
    PARTY `s 23(2) the employer`
    MUST `s 23(2) pay the total salary due to the employee`
    WITHIN `the number of days from the day the employee terminates the contract of service to the last day for payment`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 23(2) the employer` BECAUSE "the total salary due was not paid before the expiry of the 7th day after the day on which the employee terminated the contract of service"

