§§ `s 24 Income tax clearance`

-- Section 68(7) of the Income Tax Act 1947 is not among the sources: whether the
-- Comptroller of Income Tax has given permission is a fact the caller states.
-- src:1366 | 24.—(1) Despite sections 22 and 23, no payment of salary or any
-- src:1367 | other sum due to an employee on termination of service is to be made
-- src:1368 | to the employee by the employer without the permission of the
-- src:1369 | Comptroller of Income Tax under section 68(7) of the Income Tax
-- src:1370 | Act 1947.
@ref s 24(1) (src:1366-1370)
GIVEN `the Comptroller of Income Tax has given permission under section 68(7) of the Income Tax Act 1947` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 24(1) payment of the salary or other sum due on termination of service is to be made to the employee by the employer` MEANS
    IF `the Comptroller of Income Tax has given permission under section 68(7) of the Income Tax Act 1947`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "no payment of salary or any other sum due to an employee on termination of service is to be made to the employee by the employer without the permission of the Comptroller" -- with permission the subsection does not say the payment is to be made; sections 22 and 23 do
    THEN NOTHING
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "no payment of salary or any other sum due to an employee on termination of service is to be made to the employee by the employer without the permission of the Comptroller of Income Tax" -- marginal (a)
    ELSE JUST FALSE

DECLARE `s 24(1) Actor` IS ONE OF
    `s 24(1) the employer`

DECLARE `s 24(1) Action` IS ONE OF
    `s 24(1) pay the salary or other sum due to the employee on termination of service without the Comptroller's permission`

-- The prohibition of subsection (1), derived from the flat negative (ruling N2): the employer
-- shall not pay without the permission.  Doing it is the breach.
@ref s 24(1) (src:1366-1370)
GIVEN `the Comptroller of Income Tax has given permission under section 68(7) of the Income Tax Act 1947` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 24(1) Actor` `s 24(1) Action`
`s 24(1) the employer's prohibition on paying without the Comptroller's permission` MEANS
    IF NOT `the Comptroller of Income Tax has given permission under section 68(7) of the Income Tax Act 1947`
    THEN PARTY `s 24(1) the employer`
         SHANT `s 24(1) pay the salary or other sum due to the employee on termination of service without the Comptroller's permission`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `s 24(1) the employer` BECAUSE "the employer paid the salary or other sum due on termination of service without the permission of the Comptroller of Income Tax"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- "the notice has been given to and received by the Comptroller": the day the notice both
-- was given and was received.
-- src:1374 | (2) The employer must immediately give notice of the termination
-- src:1375 | of service to the Comptroller of Income Tax and the payment of the
-- src:1376 | salary or other sum due to the employee must not be delayed more
-- src:1377 | than 30 days after the notice has been given to and received by the
-- src:1378 | Comptroller of Income Tax.
@ref s 24(2) (src:1374-1378)
GIVEN `the day the notice of termination of service was given to and received by the Comptroller of Income Tax` IS A DATE
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 24(2) the last day by which the payment of the salary or other sum due must be made` MEANS
    `the last day of a period of days from the event` `the day the notice of termination of service was given to and received by the Comptroller of Income Tax` 30 `the public holidays` FALSE

@ref s 24(2) (src:1374-1378)
GIVEN `the day the notice of termination of service was given to and received by the Comptroller of Income Tax` IS A DATE
      `the day the salary or other sum due was paid` IS A DATE
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 24(2) the payment was not delayed more than 30 days after the notice was given to and received by the Comptroller` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 24(2) the last day by which the payment of the salary or other sum due must be made` `the day the notice of termination of service was given to and received by the Comptroller of Income Tax` `the public holidays`
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the count of days comes from the Interpretation Act module, which gives no answer
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST last THEN JUST (`the day the salary or other sum due was paid` AT MOST last)

DECLARE `s 24(2) Actor` IS ONE OF
    `s 24(2) the employer`

DECLARE `s 24(2) Action` IS ONE OF
    `s 24(2) give notice of the termination of service to the Comptroller of Income Tax`

@ref s 24(2) (src:1374-1378)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 24(2) Actor` `s 24(2) Action`
`s 24(2) the employer's duty to give the Comptroller notice immediately` MEANS
    PARTY `s 24(2) the employer`
    MUST `s 24(2) give notice of the termination of service to the Comptroller of Income Tax`
    WITHIN 0
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 24(2) the employer` BECAUSE "the employer did not immediately give notice of the termination of service to the Comptroller of Income Tax"

§§ `s 25 Payment to be made during working hours`

-- src:1384 | 25.—(1) Payment of salary must be made on a working day and
-- src:1385 | during working hours at the place of work or at any other place agreed
-- src:1386 | to between the employer and the employee.
@ref s 25(1) (src:1384-1386)
GIVEN `the payment was made on a working day` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment was made during working hours` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment was made at the place of work or at another place agreed between the employer and the employee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 25(1) the payment of salary was made on a working day and during working hours at the place of work or at an agreed place` MEANS
    `the payment was made on a working day` AND `the payment was made during working hours` AND `the payment was made at the place of work or at another place agreed between the employer and the employee`

-- src:1388 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply where the salary is paid into an
-- src:1389 | account with a bank in Singapore, being an account in the name of the
-- src:1390 | employee or an account in the name of the employee jointly with one
-- src:1391 | or more other persons.
@ref s 25(2) (src:1388-1391)
GIVEN `the salary is paid into an account with a bank in Singapore, in the name of the employee or jointly with one or more other persons` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 25(2) subsection (1) applies to the payment of the salary` MEANS
    IF `the salary is paid into an account with a bank in Singapore, in the name of the employee or jointly with one or more other persons`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply where the salary is paid into an account with a bank in Singapore" -- marginal (a)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- Subsection (1) is a general rule ("Payment of salary must be made on a working day and during working hours at the place of work or at any other place agreed to between the employer and the employee") with no limit of its own, and subsection (2) removes only the bank-account case; so when (2) does not apply, (1) does (read both, 2026-11-05).
    ELSE JUST TRUE
